<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Saadaoui et al. (2020), Serra et al. (2023) & Rozbicki et al. (2015) avian gastrulation tensile ring, Polonaise twin-vortex flow & primitive streak attractor — MorphoEval overall 57.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 baseline assessment of `2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py` (58.3/100). The initial script verifies the dipolar Polonaise streamfunction circulation conservation identity `Gamma_L + Gamma_R = 0` and compares basic wild-type vs FGF-inhibited circular ring flow speeds, but uses an analytic streamfunction surrogate rather than a coupled 2D viscous epiblast Stokes PDE solver `eta*nabla^2 v + eta_b*nabla(nabla.v) = -nabla.(m Q)` paired with active nematic myosin cable advection-alignment (`Dm/Dt` and `DQ_{ij}/Dt`) and Finite-Time Lyapunov Exponent (FTLE) Lagrangian attractor skeleton computation, lacks all 5 experimental regimes (missing ectopic Vg1/Wnt twin streaks and SB431542 ingression block) and a 2D parameter morphospace, and does not perform automated computer-vision segmentation of the area pellucida, area opaca, HH1 Koller's sickle, and HH3 primitive streak on `chick_primitive_streak_specimen.jpg`. Overall 57.2/100 (faithfulness 55.2, reproducibility 62.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 59, Morphological realism / specimen match 52, Parameter expressivity 56, Morphometric validation 55, Source and data traceability 66, Code-to-model traceability 60, Reproducibility package 60. Output judged: docs/media/gastrulation_streak_attractor_comparison.png: rendered output of 2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 559229 B, 1890×616 px, artifact_sha256 c4013336b345b21ccab6836387f25f6d2c7726fa6b9bc739ea0185d7f6bba8d5 (sha256 c4013336b345b21ccab6836387f25f6d2c7726fa6b9bc739ea0185d7f6bba8d5), spec_fingerprint 394d38439dd8f3b351ba32f3eef22da12f99bfa222be7659901a95855eb8a1e1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 394d38439dd8f3b351ba32f3eef22da12f99bfa222be7659901a95855eb8a1e1; artifact_sha256: c4013336b345b21ccab6836387f25f6d2c7726fa6b9bc739ea0185d7f6bba8d5." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add automated CV segmentation of the area pellucida, area opaca, HH1 posterior Koller's sickle crescent, HH2 Polonaise PIV bilateral vortex symmetry, and HH3+ midline primitive streak on `datasets/gastrulation_streak_attractor/chick_primitive_streak_specimen.jpg`.",
        "remediation needed: Evaluate all 5 Saadaoui et al. (2020) / Serra et al. (2023) experimental regimes (`wildtype_hh1_to_hh3_polonaise_streak`, `fgf_inhibited_su5402_circular_ring`, `ectopic_vg1_wnt_twin_streaks`, `ingression_blocked_nodal_sb431542`, `rock_inhibited_y27632_flow_arrest`) and a 15x15 2D `(delta_m x beta_m)` parameter morphospace.",
        "remediation needed: Implement a coupled 2D viscous epiblast Stokes PDE solver `eta*nabla^2 v + eta_b*nabla(nabla.v) = -nabla.(m Q)` + active nematic Myosin-II cable advection-alignment (`Dm/Dt` and `DQ_{ij}/Dt`) + Finite-Time Lyapunov Exponent (FTLE) Lagrangian attractor skeleton computation on the circular chick blastoderm disc." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.72e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Saadaoui et al. (2020), Serra et al. (2023) & Rozbicki et al. (2015) avian gastrulation tensile ring, Polonaise twin-vortex flow & primitive streak attractor — Parameter expressivity: 56/100" ;
